  "raw_text": "Step 1: Let \\( x = 0.\\overline{1331} \\).\n\nStep 2: Multiply both sides by 10000 to shift the decimal point four places to the right, giving \\( 10000x = 1331.\\overline{1331} \\).\n\nStep 3: Subtract the original equation from this new equation to eliminate the repeating part:\n\\[ 10000x - x = 1331.\\overline{1331} - 0.\\overline{1331} \\]\n\\[ 9999x = 1331 \\]\n\nStep 4: Solve for \\( x \\):\n\\[ x = \\frac{1331}{9999} \\]\n\nStep 5: Simplify the fraction \\(\\frac{1331}{9999}\\) by finding the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 1331 and 9999. The GCD of 1331 and 9999 is 1331.\n\nStep 6: Divide both the numerator and the denominator by their GCD:\n\\[ \\frac{1331 \\div 1331}{9999 \\div 1331} = \\frac{1}{7.5} = \\frac{1}{7.5} \\times \\frac{2}{2} = \\frac{2}{15} \\]\n\nStep 7: Since the GCD of 1 and 15 is 1, the fraction \\(\\frac{2}{15}\\) is in its simplest form.\n\nStep 8: Add the numerator and the denominator of the simplified fraction:\n\\[ a + b = 2 + 15 = 17 \\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{17}<|im_end|>",
